The `TestACMEServerDirectory` failure is pre-existing on the baseline (environment/network-related), not caused by my change. All other tests pass.

## Summary

The bug: in `Replacer.replace` (replacer.go:139), an early-return optimization skipped all processing when the input contained no opening brace `{`. As a result, an escaped closing brace `\}` — e.g. from `uri replace "\}" %7D` in the Caddyfile — was passed through with its backslash intact instead of being unescaped to `}`, so the substring replacement never matched closing brackets.

The fix makes the early return also check for an escaped closing brace (`\}`), letting the existing escaped-brace scan strip the backslash:

```go
if !strings.Contains(input, string(phOpen)) {
    // if there's no placeholder opening, then the only thing that
    // could be replaced is an escaped closing brace, so check for that
    if !strings.Contains(input, string(phEscape)+string(phClose)) {
        return input, nil
    }
}
```

Verified:
- `TestReplacer` previously-failing cases (`\}` → `}`, `\\}` → `\}`) now pass
- End-to-end `TestUriReplace` integration test passes (`?test={%20content%20}` → `test=%7B%20content%20%7D`)
- `caddyfile_adapt` tests, root package, `caddyconfig/...`, and `rewrite` module tests all pass
